      "content": "Your goal is to be direct and avoid vague political science jargon.\n\nHere are the most pragmatic arguments to challenge Democratic Socialist policies in a real-world context:\n\n1.  **Utility of \"Politicians over the Party\"**: You can argue that the \"democracy\" in democratic socialism often fails the people because voter priorities and party loyalty often contradict each other, and politicians rarely side with the most radical factions of the party.\n2.  **The Politician's Party**: Politicians typically prioritize party loyalty over the needs of the individual party member, leading to policies that favor a specific group of voters over the broader public.\n3.  **The \"Politician\" vs. \"The Party\"**: This distinction is often a smokescreen for politicians to act untruthfully to the party they represent, using party rhetoric to silence critics while pursuing personal or factional interests.\n\nYou should focus on these practical failures of leadership and policy execution when presenting to your donors.",
